Review a schema migration for safety risks

Usage: relune review [OPTIONS] <--before <FILE>|--before-sql-text <TEXT>|--before-schema-json <FILE>> <--after <FILE>|--after-sql-text <TEXT>|--after-schema-json <FILE>>

Options:
      --before <FILE>
          Baseline SQL or schema JSON file

  -c, --config <CONFIG>
          Path to configuration file (TOML; merges with CLI flags)

      --before-sql-text <TEXT>
          Baseline SQL DDL directly from a string

      --color <COLOR>
          Colorize output

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colorize if output is a terminal
          - always: Always colorize output
          - never:  Never colorize output
          
          [default: auto]

      --before-schema-json <FILE>
          Baseline normalized schema JSON file

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (can be repeated)

      --after <FILE>
          Updated SQL or schema JSON file

  -q, --quiet
          Reduce non-error output

      --after-sql-text <TEXT>
          Updated SQL DDL directly from a string

      --after-schema-json <FILE>
          Updated normalized schema JSON file

      --dialect <DIALECT>
          SQL dialect for parsing (auto-detected if omitted)

          Possible values:
          - auto:     Automatically detect dialect from SQL content
          - postgres: `PostgreSQL` dialect
          - mysql:    `MySQL` dialect
          - sqlite:   `SQLite` dialect

  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format. Defaults to `text` after config merge

          Possible values:
          - text:     Human-readable text output
          - markdown: GitHub-flavored Markdown output
          - json:     JSON output

  -o, --out <FILE>
          Output file path; stdout if omitted

      --rules <RULE>
          Restrict execution to specific rules (can be repeated)

      --except-rule <RULE>
          Remove specific rules from the active rule set (can be repeated)

      --except-table <PATTERN>
          Suppress findings for matching tables (can be repeated, supports `*`)

      --deny <SEVERITY>
          Minimum severity that causes non-zero exit

          Possible values:
          - info:     Information-only findings
          - warning:  Warning-level findings (semantic shifts)
          - caution:  Caution-level findings (operational risk)
          - breaking: Breaking findings (migration is expected to fail)

      --exit-code
          Exit with code 10 if any findings are emitted

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
